## From TASK_06 — Add Save-Version Migration Layer

### `parseImportFile` version-rejection test uses FileReader (browser-only)
- `src/export.ts` `parseImportFile` uses `FileReader`, which is unavailable in
  the Node/vitest environment. The version-rejection contract is therefore
  tested indirectly in `src/migration.test.ts` by asserting the guard
  predicate (`version > CURRENT_SAVE_VERSION`) and that `migrateSaveFile`
  does not silently downgrade a future-version save.
- **Out of scope for TASK_06**: a full end-to-end `parseImportFile` test
  would require a jsdom/MockFileReader setup. A follow-up could add a
  browser-environment test (e.g. `// @vitest-environment jsdom`) that
  exercises the actual `FileReader` path.

### `migrateWorldLineTypes` / `migrateWorldMotion` still exported from `importHelpers.ts`
- These helpers are now only consumed by `src/migration.ts` (and
  `remapImportedWorld` keeps a per-plate `migrateLineType` safety net). They
  are no longer called directly from `main.ts`.
- They are kept as the building blocks the migration pipeline composes; the
  `remapImportedWorld` `migrateLineType` call is intentionally retained as an
  idempotent safety net per the task brief.
- **Out of scope**: folding `migrateWorldLineTypes` / `migrateWorldMotion`
  directly into `migration.ts` would couple the migration module to
  `importHelpers` internals; leaving them as the composable primitives is
  fine. A future cleanup could inline them if `importHelpers` is split
  further.

### v1 → v2 migration step is a no-op
- No structural change between save v1 and v2 is known (the line-type rename
  landed at v3 and the motion model at v4). The v1→v2 step in
  `migrateSaveFile` only bumps the version number so older saves flow
  through the later steps.
- **Out of scope**: if git archaeology reveals a real v1→v2 transformation,
  it should be added to the v1→v2 block in `src/migration.ts`.
